    "body": "For anyone sharing the same use case, I'm working around this by putting the following snippet at the end of my `.zshrc`.\r\n_note that I'm using `gxargs` which is the gnu version of xargs for MacOS_\r\n```bash\r\n# begin starship\r\neval \"$(starship init zsh)\"\r\n\r\neval \"$(typeset -f prompt_starship_precmd | sed -E '1s/^(.)/t_\\1/')\"\r\nprompt_starship_precmd() {\r\n  t_prompt_starship_precmd\r\n  if [ \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2> /dev/null)\" = \"$HOME\" ]; then\r\n    echo -n git_{branch,status} | gxargs -d\\  -I{} starship config {}.disabled true\r\n  else\r\n    echo -n git_{branch,status} | gxargs -d\\  -I{} starship config {}.disabled false\r\n  fi\r\n}\r\n# end starship\r\n```",
